      "parsed_output": {
        "files_changed": [
          "src/main/java/org/codehaus/plexus/archiver/AbstractUnArchiver.java",
          "src/test/java/org/codehaus/plexus/archiver/tar/TarUnArchiverPathTraversalTest.java"
        ],
        "patch_notes": "In AbstractUnArchiver.extractFile, immediately after `final File f = FileUtils.resolveFile( dir, entryName )`, added a guard that compares canonical paths: it computes `dir.getCanonicalPath() + File.separator` and `f.getCanonicalPath()`, and throws `ArchiverException(\"Entry is outside of the target directory (\" + entryName + \")\")` unless the resolved file's canonical path starts with the destination directory's canonical path. This is the single shared extraction sink for both the tar path (TarUnArchiver -> extractFile) and the zip path (AbstractZipUnArchiver -> extractFileIfIncluded -> extractFile) reported in the alert, so one change covers all traces. The separator is appended to the directory prefix to avoid sibling-prefix false negatives (e.g. /tmp/dest vs /tmp/dest-evil). getCanonicalPath throws IOException, which extractFile already declares. Added TarUnArchiverPathTraversalTest which builds a tar containing a \"../evil.txt\" entry, asserts extraction throws ArchiverException, and asserts the file is not written outside the destination directory.",
        "regression_commands": [
          "mvn -B -Dtest=TarUnArchiverPathTraversalTest test",
          "mvn -B -Dtest=TarUnArchiverTest,ZipUnArchiverTest test"
        ],
        "risk_notes": "The check uses canonical paths, which resolve symlinks; legitimate extractions (including existing symlink tests) still pass — full suite is 150 tests, 0 failures, 1 pre-existing skip. Malicious entries now throw ArchiverException instead of silently escaping, which is the intended hardening.",
        "status": "patched",
        "summary": "Fixed a \"Zip Slip\" path traversal (CWE-022) in plexus-archiver. Archive entry names (from tar/zip) were passed unchecked to FileUtils.resolveFile in AbstractUnArchiver.extractFile, so an entry like \"../evil.txt\" would resolve outside the destination directory and be written/created there (mkdirs, FileOutputStream, symlink). Added a canonical-path containment check that rejects any entry resolving outside the destination directory before any filesystem write."
      }
    }
  ],
